Pichhle lesson mein humne Promise.all() seekha tha. Ab 3 aur methods seekhenge jo real-world API calls mein useful hain.
1. Promise.allSettled() — Sabka result chahiye
Maan lo 3 API calls hain aur ek fail ho jaati hai. Tum phir bhi baaki sabka result chahte ho.
const results = await Promise.allSettled([
  Promise.resolve("Users loaded"),
  Promise.reject("Products failed"),
  Promise.resolve("Orders loaded")
]);

console.log(results);


Output ka simplified version:
[
  { status: "fulfilled", value: "Users loaded" },
  { status: "rejected", reason: "Products failed" },
  { status: "fulfilled", value: "Orders loaded" }
]


Har Promise ka apna result ya error milta hai.
Use case: Dashboard mein multiple services ka status dikhana, bhale hi koi ek service fail ho jaye.
2. Promise.race() — Jo pehle settle ho
Jo Promise sabse pehle successful ho ya fail ho, uska result race() decide karta hai.
const result = await Promise.race([
  new Promise<string>(resolve =>
    setTimeout(() => resolve("API 1"), 1000)
  ),
  new Promise<string>(resolve =>
    setTimeout(() => resolve("API 2"), 500)
  )
]);

console.log(result);


Output:
API 2


Kyunki API 2 500 milliseconds mein complete hui, jabki API 1 ko 1000 milliseconds lage.
Important: race() mein pehla settled Promise jeetta hai. Agar sabse pehle reject hua, toh race() bhi reject hoga.
3. Promise.any() — Pehli successful response
Maan lo tum ek hi data ke liye multiple servers try kar rahe ho. Tumhe pehli successful response chahiye.
const result = await Promise.any([
  Promise.reject("Server 1 failed"),
  Promise.resolve("Server 2 success"),
  Promise.resolve("Server 3 success")
]);

console.log(result);


Output:
Server 2 success


Promise.any() errors ko ignore karta hai jab tak koi Promise successfully fulfill na ho. Agar saare reject ho jaayen, toh AggregateError throw hota hai.
4. Quick comparison
Method	Kya wait karta hai?	Kab useful hai?
Promise.all()	Sab successful hon	Sab results required hon
Promise.allSettled()	Sab settle hon	Har task ka outcome chahiye
Promise.race()	Pehla settled result	Fastest result ya timeout pattern
Promise.any()	Pehli successful response	Multiple servers mein fallback
